course: dictionary
lesson: 9392
title: Tiny jumpers in the soil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A springtail is a very small animal, so small you may need a magnifying glass to see it. It has no wings and six legs, and it lives in soil and under fallen leaves. The word itself gives a clue: spring and tail.
explain: You can use context to work out what springtails are. «Trap-jaw ants lock their jaws open and snap them shut, catching quick prey like springtails.» Prey means animals that are hunted for food, so springtails are small creatures that ants catch and eat.
explain: Always test your meaning. Try it in the sentence: "Trap-jaw ants catch quick prey like tiny soil animals that jump." It still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: A springtail is a tiny, wingless, six-legged animal that lives in soil and leaf litter.
fact: Leaf litter is the layer of dead leaves that covers the ground in a wood or garden.
fact: Springtails jump by flicking a spring-like tail under their body.
fact: Springtails break down dead leaves, which helps make soil.
fact: Springtails are harmless to people, and «trap-jaw ants» catch them as prey.
exercise: «Trap-jaw ants lock their jaws open and snap them shut, catching quick prey like springtails.» What are springtails in this sentence? | Quick prey caught by ants | Large birds that eat ants | Plants that grow in the soil | *Small creatures that ants catch for food
exercise: A springtail jumps away from danger. What does it jump with? | Its six wings | Its long neck | *Its spring-like tail | Its strong jaws
exercise: Where would you most likely find a springtail? | On top of a tall mountain | *Under dead leaves in the soil | Inside a fish tank | High in the clouds
test: How many legs does a springtail have? | Four | *Six | Ten | Eight
test: Which statement about springtails is true? | They have wings and fly | They are dangerous to people | They are as big as a dog | *They are tiny, wingless and harmless to people
exam: Why are springtails helpful to soil? | They grow big roots | They make the soil go hard | *They break down dead leaves and help make soil | They pump water out of the ground
